#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Step 11 Report: the lab's report page renders only from step 08's manifest, step 10's Results and the deal and
settlement records they cite, every number on it has a denominator, nothing on it is a score, and the page's byte
digest is sealed in the reporting node's book.

Usage: 11-report --population DIR --out RUN/11-report
       11-report --population DIR --preview-open-month --run RUN --out PREVIEW/11-report [--page FILE]

RUN is the loop run (the parent of --out). The only record bytes this step reads
are the deal and settlement records 10's Results cite, for the exchanges figure:

  inputs        08's finding passes steps/finding.py's check and names its
                manifest in proof. 10's finding does too, and is PASS. Each of
                10's bundles is VALID under `capsulectl verify --bundle` and
                under the repository's judge key, the roll-up cites exactly the
                finer Results, and every record they cite has the sha256 08's
                manifest gives it, in a step 08 reproduced. An input that does
                not hold is a FAIL and nothing is rendered.
  figures       counted from those inputs: records and steps per kind, each
                pack term's outcomes, the roll-up, and paid exchanges. 10's
                Results judge per step, so paid exchanges are counted from the
                contents of the records they cite, each matching 08's digest: a
                paid exchange is one payer's sealed deal, the only deal record
                there is (capsules-plugin#134 owns the provider's), and an
                exchange is one exchange id. A file no Result cites counts for
                nothing. Each figure cites its records by digest.
  page          the figures are sealed as one report Result, and the pinned
                `capsulectl book report build --seal` renders it and seals the
                page's sha256 in the reporting book. The finding commits
                report.json and the page's sha256, not the page (--page leaves
                a local copy); report.json names the pinned builder versions.
  checks        seal         `book report check` says match, and the disclosed
                             seal record holds the page's sha256;
                denominators every number in a figure is "k of n", k <= n;
                no score     no score, rank, rating or leaderboard field or word
                             in the page's data. The builder's viewer script is
                             pinned code and is not scanned.
                rebuilds     two rebuilds of the page have the same bytes, and
                             they are the sealed bytes;
                result bundle   the report Result's bundle verifies;
                no paid product  no enterprise or paid-product text in the page.

The reporting book is, on rehearsal, a scratch book under the repository's TEST
reporter key (population/<p>/step11/keys). On live it is the first node's join
book (book_dir, profile named for the node), under its key in data_dir.

A rehearsal run with neither 08-verify/ nor 10-judge/ runs step 10 into
OUT/standin/10-judge, which judges the committed stand-in run, and the detail
says so. Live records are collected by the operator from the lab's own nodes,
never through a peer; a live run without 08's and 10's outputs is NOT_CHECKED.

--preview-open-month (evidence-network/loop#242) reports over step 10's open-month preview, PREVIEW/10-judge (written by
`10-judge --preview-open-month --run RUN`), with 08's manifest and the records from RUN (--run). The only 10-judge it
accepts is a preview one judged from RUN's own 08 manifest (window.json names its sha256), and a run without
--preview-open-month refuses a preview one. It is never a baseline result:
it writes only --out (outside RUN and findings/), never runs step 10 itself, and every finding it writes has a detail
that starts with finding.PREVIEW, which the ecosystem gate refuses.

The design is steps/11-report.md. Exit 0 once the finding is written.
"""
